</addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKENAGA, SHIGENOBU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKO, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUI CHEMICALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, RYOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIZONO, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKENAGA SHIGENOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANEKO KAZUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORI RYOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORIZONO KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKENAGA, SHIGENOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKO, KAZUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, RYOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIZONO, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Flexible syndiotactic polypropylene compositions having an excellent balance among transparency, flexibility, heat resistance, etc.; and a laminate comprising a layer made of any of the compositions and a layer made of a thermoplastic resin. One composition (1) comprises a syndiotactic propylene polymer (A), an  DOLLAR (g)a-olefin polymer (B), and a small amount of a nucleating agent (C) and/or an ethylene polymer (D). Another composition (2) comprises the polymer (A), the polymer (B), an isotactic propylene polymer (E), and a small amount of the nucleating agent (C) and/or the polymer (D). Still another composition (3) comprises the polymer (A), the polymer (B), the polymer (E), a copolymer of a vinyl compound having a polar group and ethylene (F), and a small amount of the polymer (D).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne des compositions polymères syndiotactiques souples présentant un excellent rapport entre transparence, flexibilité et résistance à la chaleur notamment, et un stratifié comprenant une couche réalisée dans la composition susmentionnée et une couche de résine thermoplastique. Une composition (1) comprend un polymère de propylène syndioactique (A), un polymère d' alpha -oléfine (B) et une faible quantité d'agent nucléant (C) et/ou d'un polymère d'éthylène (D). Une autre composition (2) comprend un polymère (A), le polymère (B), un polymère de propylène isotactique (E) et une faible quantité d'agent nucléant (C) et/ou de polymère (D). Une autre composition encore comprend le polymère (A), le polymère (E), un copolymère d'un composé vinylique avec groupe polaire et un éthylène (F), ainsi qu'une faible quantité de polymère (D).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>